WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.400
Why does the crow take the chosen undead to Lordran?

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.040
Oscar speaks of a prophecy in which the chosed undead must escape the asylum.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.100
It's easy to say that the crow is just a meaningless method of transport,

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.300
but perhaps the story is deeper than that.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.660
Gargoyles guard the bell of awakening, bat demons take you from Sen's fortress to Anor Londo,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.800
and snake men are used as guards.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.500
The lords seemed to have the ability to make beasts do their bidding.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.400
There is one goddess in particular who has a powerful link with crows.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:55.840
Velka.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.340
In Japanese mythology crows are messengers from the gods,

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.900
symbolizing divine intervention and guidance on human affairs.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.520
The crow takes you to Lordran where you become manipulated by the gods.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.920
So if we assume that Velka is linked to the giant crow, or IS the crow

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.360
we have to ask: Why would she want powerful undead to escape the asylum?

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.320
Velka is the goddess of sin,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.780
it's worth noting that she doesn't have a lord soul, but is an actual goddess.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.580
She does not just punish humans,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.500
she has a great degree of influence where the gods are concerned.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.100
And the lords fear her.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.040
Everything related to Velka, and everything that the lords fear,

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.840
is locked away in the painted world of Ariamis.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.120
In the painted world there are hundreds of crows,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.320
there are the crowpeople of Velka,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.700
there is the equipment of Velkas partners,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.940
and there are the spells used by her order.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.340
Most importantly however, the painted world holds everything that the lords fear.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.400
It holds the occult ember, and the half-dragon Priscilla.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.720
Both of which are lethal to the lords.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.240
So with all this information we are left guessing the allegiance of Velka.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.680
Why is she taking undead from the asylum to Lordran?

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.640
The vow of silence miracle describes Velka as a rogue deity,

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.180
suggesting she has no allegiance save the hunting down of sinners.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.120
Perhaps by taking you to Lordran she is unleashing you upon the gods for their sins.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.340
The chosen undead certainly is a nightmare for any gods he encounters,

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.660
attacking them relentlessly until he succeeds, not even letting death stop him.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.060
I think having someone unkillable come at you over and over again is pretty good punishment.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.820
Perhaps Velka is on Gwyndolin's side,

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:50.940
Gwyndolin is the leader of the darkmoons, who hunt down sinners inside Velka's book of the guilty.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.940
Gwyndolin wants to find worthy undead to link the flame,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:00.300
and Velka could simply be a part of that, since she chooses powerful undead from the asylum through her crow.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.480
Interpretation number 3 is your own interpretation.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.780
I can't say I'm right and I can't say you're wrong, because the game is open-ended and it's fun to speculate.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.760
So based on this information, do you think Velka has a hidden role in the plot?

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.360
Is she playing her hand from behind the scenes? Why?

